{"assets":["/statement-assets/b91801854be41f70e8f03baa1d51c09ea4f81ff1d2b1619c41e133487b335ba1.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1691","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. K-Set Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree $$$G$$$ with $$$n$$$ vertices and an integer $$$k$$$. The vertices of the tree are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a vertex $$$r$$$ and a subset $$$S$$$ of vertices of $$$G$$$, such that $$$|S| = k$$$, we define $$$f(r, S)$$$ as the size of the smallest rooted subtree containing all vertices in $$$S$$$ when the tree is rooted at $$$r$$$. A set of vertices $$$T$$$ is called a rooted subtree, if all the vertices in $$$T$$$ are connected, and for each vertex in $$$T$$$, all its descendants belong to $$$T$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to calculate the sum of $$$f(r, S)$$$ over "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all possible distinct combinations"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of vertices $$$r$$$ and subsets $$$S$$$, where $$$|S| = k$$$. Formally, compute the following: $$$$$$\\sum_{r \\in V} \\sum_{S \\subseteq V, |S| = k} f(r, S),$$$$$$ where $$$V$$$ is the set of vertices in $$$G$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the answer modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following $$$n - 1$$$ lines contains two integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ ($$$1 \\le x, y \\le n$$$), denoting an edge between vertex $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the answer modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2\n1 2\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n25\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 2\n1 2\n2 3\n2 4\n1 5\n4 6\n4 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n849\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The tree in the second example is given below:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b91801854be41f70e8f03baa1d51c09ea4f81ff1d2b1619c41e133487b335ba1.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We have $$$21$$$ subsets of size $$$2$$$ in the given tree. Hence, $$$$$$S \\in \\left\\{\\{1, 2\\}, \\{1, 3\\}, \\{1, 4\\}, \\{1, 5\\}, \\{1, 6\\}, \\{1, 7\\}, \\{2, 3\\}, \\{2, 4\\}, \\{2, 5\\}, \\{2, 6\\}, \\{2, 7\\}, \\{3, 4\\}, \\{3, 5\\}, \\{3, 6\\}, \\{3, 7\\}, \\{4, 5\\}, \\{4, 6\\}, \\{4, 7\\}, \\{5, 6\\}, \\{5, 7\\}, \\{6, 7\\} \\right\\}.$$$$$$ And since we have $$$7$$$ vertices, $$$1 \\le r \\le 7$$$. We need to find the sum of $$$f(r, S)$$$ over all possible pairs of $$$r$$$ and $$$S$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below we have listed the value of $$$f(r, S)$$$ for some combinations of $$$r$$$ and $$$S$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$r = 1$$$, $$$S = \\{3, 7\\}$$$. The value of $$$f(r, S)$$$ is $$$5$$$ and the corresponding subtree is $$$\\{2, 3, 4, 6, 7\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$r = 1$$$, $$$S = \\{5, 4\\}$$$. The value of $$$f(r, S)$$$ is $$$7$$$ and the corresponding subtree is $$$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$r = 1$$$, $$$S = \\{4, 6\\}$$$. The value of $$$f(r, S)$$$ is $$$3$$$ and the corresponding subtree is $$$\\{4, 6, 7\\}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1691F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1691/problem/F"}